  "id": "aquapolis-booster-box",
  "name": "Aquapolis booster box",
  "category": "product_promotion",
  "description": {
    "text": "Sealed Aquapolis booster boxes, from January 2003, each came with one oversized box topper lying on top of the packs, a jumbo copy of one of four of the set's holo rares: Entei, Espeon, Scizor or Suicune. They are 5/12 to 8/12 in the run of twelve box toppers Wizards of the Coast gave its e-Card series, and PSA grades them as a set of their own, Aquapolis Box Topper.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Flipside Gaming: Retrospective, Aquapolis (2017)",
        "url": "https://flipsidegaming.com/blogs/pokemon-blog/retrospective-aquapolis"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: the e-Card box toppers and the clear plastic Skyridge cards",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/does-anyone-remember-the-clear-plastic-cards/10584"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: List of all English sets recognized by PSA",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/list-of-all-english-sets-recognized-by-psa/30868"
      },
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: Box Topper (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 27 July 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260727023621/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Box_Topper_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
